<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bornholm</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bornholm is a Danish island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>. It was ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-roskilde">Treaty of Roskilde</a> in 1658, together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blekinge">Blekinge</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halland">Halland</a> and Norwegian provinces, at the height of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>. The islanders rebelled against Swedish rule and Bornholm was returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in 1660.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bornholm.jpg" alt="Bornholm" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lilly M real name Małgorzata Miłaszewska · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wybrze%C5%BCe_Bornholmu.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
